# Verify trust-engine artifact signatures before pushing.
# Runs the public verify-attestations.ts (tracked, no dependency on the
# private scripts/attestation/* signer). Skips silently when no .sig
# files exist (early-bootstrap state).
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify` if you intentionally rotated keys
# and the new signatures haven't landed yet.
set -e

# Skip in CI — CI runs the same verifier as a dedicated workflow step.
[ -n "$CI" ] && exit 0

# Formatting, the way CI checks it: the WHOLE tree, not just staged files.
# ADDED 2026-08-14, after `format:check` failed in CI twice in one session
# while every local gate was green. lint-staged only formats files that are
# STAGED, so anything reaching the tree another way — a merge, a generated
# artifact copied in by a build script, a file written by a tool — is never
# formatted locally and is only caught after a push. On this repo a CI round
# trip is 20+ minutes; this check takes about forty seconds.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify`.
npm run format:check

# Every file a workflow step will execute must actually be IN the repository.
# ADDED 2026-08-10, after this failed for the FOURTH time. `.gitignore` has a
# blanket `scripts/*`, and `git add` on an ignored path is a silent no-op — so a
# commit can add a ci.yml step plus a package.json entry with no file behind
# them, stay green on every local run, and fail in CI with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND
# naming a file the author can see in their own tree. Prior occurrences:
# 2026-07-10 (validators), 2026-08-02 (role-board CTAs), 2026-08-09 (role-board
# coverage), 2026-08-10 (the three B+ remediation gates).
# Deliberately here and NOT in ci.yml: a CI step that checks whether CI's own
# files are present can only run once they are. Runs in about a second.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify`.
npm run audit:ci-workflow-files

if [ -f public/data/revisions.jsonl.sig ] || [ -f public/data/rag-corpus.json.sig ]; then
  npx tsx scripts/ci/verify-attestations.ts
fi

# Full data-integrity validator (N1-N24/CM-*/TP-*/MP-*/DS*/GC-*, 142 checks).
# ADDED 2026-07-13 — this suite (also gate:data's final step) was found to
# have never run anywhere in CI. Deliberately kept local-only rather than
# added as a GitHub Actions step: this repo's CI is already a long,
# multi-step job, and the explicit preference here is to keep GitHub CI
# runtime light — real data-integrity gating belongs at push time, on the
# machine that actually has it, not as more GHA minutes.
# TP-1 and MP-2 verify genuine on-disk presence of files under gitignored
# pqctoday-priv/local-evidence-cache/ — excluded here for the same reason
# they're excluded from every other invocation of this suite: they're real
# and useful after a manual download run, but this hook fires on every
# push regardless of whether one just happened.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify` for an intentional WIP push.
npm run validate:data -- --exclude-checks TP-1,MP-2

# WASM provenance drift — are the vendored crypto bundles still built from
# the pqctoday-hsm commit they claim?
# ADDED 2026-08-02. `sync:wasm:check` already existed as an npm script but was
# wired into nothing, so drift accumulated silently: an audit that day found 5
# of 6 bundles stale, the worst by 26 commits, meaning the HSM Workshop, TPM
# bridge, MLS and SSH simulator all ran a two-week-old engine missing a
# C_Login TOCTOU fix among others. Nobody had a signal.
# Local-only on purpose, same reasoning as the validator above: the check is a
# no-op unless a sibling ../pqctoday-hsm checkout exists, so it can only do
# real work on a machine that actually has the engine source — which is
# exactly where a rebuild would be performed.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify`.
npm run sync:wasm:check

# CACP (crypto-agility control plane) suite — the KMIP policy engine's wasm
# bridge, visual editor, and policy library. ADDED 2026-08-28 (gaps-
# remediation plan WS-10), after `gate:cacp` was found to exist in
# package.json but be wired into nothing: `gate:local`'s bare `npm run test`
# already covers this tree's CI-visible tests, but the *.local.test.ts
# drift guards (catalog ↔ Rust-grammar, dual-form policy parity,
# sim ↔ engine parity) and the narrow cacp-kmip wasm-provenance check ran
# nowhere at push time. Some of those drift guards are no-ops without a
# sibling ../pqctoday-hsm checkout (same convention as `sync:wasm:check`
# above) — see TESTING.md's CACP section. Runs unconditionally, matching
# every other check in this hook, rather than path-scoped to the CACP
# directories the plan named: the scoped test run itself is a couple of
# seconds, and path-scoping would be new machinery this hook doesn't use
# anywhere else, for a saving that small.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify`.
npm run gate:cacp

# Silent row loss between two generations of a dated CSV.
# ADDED 2026-08-14, after a near-miss that NOTHING else could have caught. Two
# sessions each wrote a new generation of library_*.csv; because dated
# generations are different FILENAMES, git merged both with no conflict, and
# the loader serves only the newest — so two rows present in one and absent
# from the other simply disappeared. No conflict, no error, no failing test.
# A human noticed.
# Local-only, matching the two gates above: it reads src/data/ and
# src/data/archive/ (the archival gate keeps only 2 live copies, so the
# previous generation is often archived) and needs no network.
# A removal that is genuinely intended is recorded in RECORDED_REMOVALS inside
# the script, with a written reason — that is the escape hatch, not disabling
# this line.
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify`.
npm run audit:csv-copy-forward
